  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "A sphere of radius $R$ has a volume density of charge $\\rho=k r,$ where $r$ is the distance from the centre of the sphere and $k$ is constant. The magnitude of the electric field which exists at the surface of the sphere is given by $\\left(\\varepsilon_{0}=\\right.$ permittivity of free space)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7sNYV",
      "text": "$\\frac{4 \\pi k R^{4}}{3 \\varepsilon_{0}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3c0XU",
      "text": "$\\frac{k R}{3 e_{0}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "lro8s",
      "text": "$\\frac{4 \\pi k R}{\\varepsilon_{0}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PmJtY",
      "text": "$\\frac{k R^{2}}{4 \\varepsilon_{0}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "By Gauss's theorem\r\n\\(\\begin{aligned} \\mathrm{E}\\left(4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^{2}\\right) &=\\frac{\\int \\mathrm{p} \\times 4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^{2} \\mathrm{dr}}{\\varepsilon_{0}} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\int \\mathrm{kr} \\times 4 \\pi \\mathrm{r}^{2} \\mathrm{dr}}{\\varepsilon_{0}} \\\\ &=\\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\mathrm{Kr}^{2}}{4 \\varepsilon_{0}} \\end{aligned}\\)",
